+
+## Help Pages as Markdown
+
+{meth}`Command.get_help_markdown` returns the help page of a command as Markdown, for reference docs that stay in sync
+with the code. The command formats its help as usual, with a {class}`MarkdownHelpFormatter` instead of the terminal
+formatter, so every section of `--help` is there, in the same order, including sections that a custom
+{meth}`Command.format_help` writes.
+
+```python
+@click.command()
+@click.option("--count", default=1, show_default=True, help="Number of greetings.")
+@click.argument("name")
+def hello(count, name):
+    """Say hello."""
+
+with click.Context(hello, info_name="hello") as ctx:
+    print(hello.get_help_markdown(ctx))
+```
+
+```markdown
+# hello
+
+Usage: `hello [OPTIONS] NAME`
+
+Say hello.
+
+## Options
+
+| Name | Description | Details |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `--count INTEGER` | Number of greetings. | default: 1 |
+| `--help` | Show this message and exit. |  |
+```
+
+The `Details` column holds the items of the bracket at the end of the help line, as `--help` shows them. Style codes
+are removed, long texts are not wrapped, and `|` is escaped.
